  <fragment slot="content">
    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>What This Tool Shows</h2>
      <p>This converter fetches live mid-market exchange rates and converts between 160+ world currencies instantly. Use it to check the real exchange rate before your bank or exchange service adds their markup — the difference can be significant on larger amounts.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>How to Get the Best Exchange Rate</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Use a no-foreign-transaction-fee credit card:</strong> Cards like Chase Sapphire, Capital One Venture, and many travel cards charge 0% foreign transaction fees and use near-market rates.</li>
        <li><strong>Withdraw from ATMs abroad:</strong> Use a debit card with low international ATM fees. Always choose to be charged in the local currency — selecting "your home currency" triggers Dynamic Currency Conversion with terrible rates.</li>
        <li><strong>Avoid airport exchanges:</strong> Airport kiosks charge 7–10% margins. If you must have cash on arrival, exchange a small amount and get the rest from ATMs.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare online services:</strong> Wise (formerly TransferWise), Revolut, and similar services offer mid-market rates with small transparent fees — often 0.3–0.5%.</li>
        <li><strong>Time large conversions:</strong> For significant amounts, monitor rates over a few days. Small fluctuations can mean hundreds of dollars on a $10,000+ conversion.</li>
      </ul>
    </div>

