          <tr><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">US Dollar</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">USD</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">United States</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">World's primary reserve currency</td></tr>
          <tr style="background:#f0fdf4;"><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Euro</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">EUR</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Eurozone (20 countries)</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Second most held reserve currency</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">British Pound</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">GBP</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">United Kingdom</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Oldest currency still in use</td></tr>
          <tr style="background:#f0fdf4;"><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Japanese Yen</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">JPY</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Japan</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Third most traded currency globally</td></tr>
          <tr><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Swiss Franc</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">CHF</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Switzerland</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Considered the ultimate "safe haven" currency</td></tr>
          <tr style="background:#f0fdf4;"><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Chinese Yuan</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;font-weight:bold;">CNY</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">China</td><td style="padding:8px;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;">Increasingly used in global trade settlements</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <FAQ items={[
      { question: "How accurate are the exchange rates?", answer: "Rates are fetched from a free exchange rate API and reflect mid-market rates. The actual rate you get from your bank or currency exchange service may differ slightly due to margins and fees." },
      { question: "How often are the rates updated?", answer: "Exchange rates are updated regularly throughout the day. However, we recommend checking with your financial institution for real-time rates on time-sensitive transactions." },
      { question: "Which currencies are supported?", answer: "This converter supports all major world currencies including USD, EUR, GBP, JPY, CAD, AUD, CHF, CNY, INR, and many more. The API provides rates for 160+ currencies worldwide." },
      { question: "Why do rates differ between banks and this converter?", answer: "This converter shows the mid-market rate — the midpoint between buy and sell prices on global currency markets. Banks add a markup (typically 1-5%) as their profit margin on currency exchanges." },
    ]} />

    <div class="content-section">
      <h2>Next Steps</h2>
      <p>Use the converter above to check the current mid-market rate before any currency exchange. If you're travelling, apply for a credit card with no foreign transaction fees at least 2–3 weeks before departure. For regular international transfers, consider setting up a Wise or Revolut account for near-market rates. Bookmark this page and check rates periodically if you're timing a large conversion — even a 1% improvement on $10,000 saves $100.</p>
    </div>
